      <h1><em>The Texas Spirits Guide: Vodka, Gin, Whiskey &amp; Agave</em></h1>
      <p class="article-meta">By the Monarch Liquor team &middot; Updated Sept 2026</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Article Body -->
    <article class="content-section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
      <div class="content-narrow prose">
        <p>There's local, then there is <strong>Texas</strong> local. Supporting Texas distillers has been part of Monarch's DNA since day one on East MLK, and the state's spirit scene has never been better. Here's our shelf-by-shelf tour of what Texas does best.</p>

        <h2>Vodka: The One That Started It All</h2>
        <p><strong>Tito's Handmade Vodka</strong> put Austin distilling on the map, and it's still the best-selling bottle in both of our stores. Corn-based, gluten-free, and smooth enough to anchor any bar cart. But don't stop there:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Deep Eddy (Austin)</strong> &mdash; famous for their Ruby Red grapefruit vodka, basically a Paloma waiting to happen.</li>
          <li><strong>Dripping Springs (Dripping Springs)</strong> &mdash; small-batch, made with Hill Country artesian water.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Gin: Hill Country Botanicals</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Waterloo Gin (Austin)</strong> &mdash; big juniper up front with pecan and lavender notes underneath; the No. 9 expression is a favorite for gin and tonics.</li>
          <li><strong>Genius Gin (Austin)</strong> &mdash; a modern, citrus-forward gin distilled just across town.</li>
          <li><strong>Dripping Springs Gin</strong> &mdash; orange-forward and friendly, great for gin newcomers.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Whiskey: Aged Under the Texas Sun</h2>
        <p>Texas heat ages whiskey fast, and the results speak for themselves. The short list:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Garrison Brothers (Hye)</strong> &mdash; Texas's first bourbon distillery. Rich, sweet, unapologetically big.</li>
          <li><strong>Still Austin (Austin)</strong> &mdash; grain-to-glass bourbon and rye made from 100% Texas grain, right here in town.</li>
          <li><strong>Balcones (Waco)</strong> &mdash; blue corn bourbon and Texas single malt with a cult following.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We went deep on these (with price tiers and picks) in our <a href="/guides/best-bourbon-whiskey-austin.html">Best Bourbon &amp; Whiskey guide</a>.</p>

        <div class="shop-callout">
          <p><strong>Shop this guide:</strong> filter by Texas brands online, or ask any associate for the local shelf tour in store.</p>
          {% order "guide-callout", "SHOP TEXAS SPIRITS", "btn-primary" %}
