        <h2>Agave &amp; Desert Spirits</h2>
        <p>Texas can't legally make tequila (that's Mexico's), but the desert spirits made here are something special:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Desert Door (Driftwood)</strong> &mdash; Texas sotol, distilled from wild-harvested desert plants. Earthy, slightly sweet, and unlike anything else &mdash; try it anywhere you'd use tequila.</li>
          <li><strong>Railean (San Leon)</strong> &mdash; Gulf Coast rum and agave spirits from a family operation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Sotol Ranch Water is a staff obsession &mdash; the recipe is in our <a href="/guides/classic-cocktails-at-home.html">cocktails guide</a>.</p>

        <h2>Why Buy Texan?</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your dollars stay with Texas farms, families, and distilleries.</li>
          <li>Local bottles make the best gifts &mdash; every one has a story.</li>
          <li>The quality now rivals (and often beats) the big national brands.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Both Monarch locations keep a dedicated local section, and we're always tasting new Texas releases. Ask us what's new &mdash; the answer changes monthly.</p>
      </div>
